# The production capability execution image for ENG-0005.
#
# NOT BUILT BY THIS REPOSITORY. No test, validator, or script builds, pulls,
# loads, or admits this. Building it is gate G5, and admitting its digest as a
# CIMP is a separate governed step an operator performs — see README.md.
#
# There is no default base. `BASE_IMAGE` has no value here on purpose: a
# floating tag baked into an authoritative definition would mean the image
# Kyri admitted and the image Kyri later built were the same text and different
# bytes. The G5 procedure supplies a digest-pinned reference and refuses
# anything that is not one, so this file cannot name a mutable base even by
# accident.
#
# The base family is the minimal runtime variant admitted at the G4 ruling of
# 2026-08-12: no shell, no package manager, and its interpreter configured at
# /usr/bin/python. T12's container command was corrected to match it rather
# than the image being deformed to preserve /usr/bin/python3, which would have
# meant carrying a package manager into the final image to create a pathname.
#
# Governed by docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-11-first-adapter-design.md §9, §27.

ARG BASE_IMAGE
FROM ${BASE_IMAGE}

# Bind-mount destinations, present in the image so that creation against a
# read-only rootfs does not depend on the runtime materialising them. WORKDIR
# is used rather than RUN mkdir because the base has no shell to run: this is
# the builder creating a directory, not a command executing inside the image.
WORKDIR /kyri/package
WORKDIR /kyri/output
WORKDIR /run/kyri/input
WORKDIR /

# Cleared deliberately. The base configures its interpreter as the entrypoint,
# and T12 passes the interpreter and the governed entrypoint as the container
# command; an inherited entrypoint would prepend a second interpreter to that
# command and the invocation would fail in a way nobody would read as a
# configuration error.
ENTRYPOINT []
CMD []

# Metadata only. The execution identity is not established here: T12 launches
# every container with an explicit `--user 1000:1000`, and the profile
# verification compares what Podman reported against that. This line states
# that the image's own default is unprivileged, so an image inspected outside
# Kyri is not mistaken for one that would run as root.
USER 65532:65532
